WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.933 --> 00:00:04.366
I’m in the project terminal, ready to start the setup.

2
00:00:06.033 --> 00:00:14.699
I run a quick masked key check to confirm "ADMIN_PK" and "AGENT_PK" are loaded, without revealing full private keys.

3
00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:21.833
Then I open a new terminal tab and go to chain/sui.

4
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:26.366
I run "sui client publish" and wait for it to finish.

5
00:00:39.933 --> 00:00:45.133
Once deployment completes, I copy the package ID for the next steps.

6
00:00:45.866 --> 00:00:48.566
Next, I run "npm run setup".

7
00:00:50.433 --> 00:00:56.300
It auto-loads the Sui private key from environment variables, so I just press Enter.

8
00:00:56.633 --> 00:01:02.966
Then I paste the package ID I copied earlier, and the agent key is also loaded from env.

9
00:01:07.666 --> 00:01:15.366
At this point we’re in the vault funding/top-up phase where we load funds into the vault for later agent use.

10
00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:38.666
At this step, I complete the vault top-up by adding the coins and amounts I need, then enter 0 to finish.

11
00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:45.933
I confirm with Y to continue strict policy setup, and then setup proceeds automatically.

12
00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:52.466
After that, runtime setup runs and installs/refreshes the plugin.

13
00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:58.566
I press Yes here to show the config step and confirm the runtime values.

14
00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:06.800
You can add the Telegram bot token and chat ID here as part of the .env configuration.

15
00:02:07.166 --> 00:02:15.066
After that, you can set an authorized Telegram username or user ID, so only approved accounts can trigger actions.

16
00:02:16.233 --> 00:02:21.733
You can also set these optional configurations here, based on your setup needs.

17
00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:33.333
Then setup completes the full flow and runs verification checks, including a wallet fetch, to confirm everything is configured correctly.

18
00:02:37.133 --> 00:02:42.033
After that, we also run "openclaw clawall wallet" to confirm it manually.

19
00:02:44.733 --> 00:02:50.000
You can run "openclaw clawall -h" to see all available commands.

20
00:02:55.166 --> 00:03:01.133
To uninstall Clawall cleanly, run "npm run uninstall:clawall".

21
00:03:05.433 --> 00:03:12.633
Then it uninstalls the plugin through OpenClaw, restarts the gateway, and performs cleanup.

22
00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:19.533
We’ll also do a manual restart afterward to make sure everything is fully refreshed.

23
00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:33.799
And that’s it, your Clawall setup is complete and ready to use.

